        "The `objective=\"reg:squarederror\"` is to indicate the loss function. The default is `\"reg:squarederror\"` that is regression with squared loss. More loss function can be found in the [documnet](https://xgboost.readthedocs.io/en/stable/parameter.html#learning-task-parameters).\n",
        "\n",
        "The most important hyperparameters are:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Parameter | Meaning |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| `n_estimators` | Number of boosting rounds. |\n",
        "| `learning_rate` | Learning rate. |\n",
        "| `max_depth` | Depth of each tree. |\n",
        "| `subsample` | Fraction of observations used for each tree. |\n",
        "| `colsample_bytree` | Fraction of predictors used for each tree. |\n",
